a is equivalent to ⊤ or ⊥. ⊤ cooperates with DefectBot, and ⊥ defects against FairBot.\n- **Depth 1:** the formula is a Boolean combination of boxes over a, c and d, so its value at world n depends only on which (a,c,d) triples occurred at worlds before n.\n  - Against CooperateBot every atom is true at every world, so X's action from world 1 on is a single value p. Prudence needs X to defect, so p = D.\n  - Against FairBot, the triple at world 0 is also (1,1,1), because the boxes are vacuously true there. So X's action against FairBot at world 1 is also p = D.\n  - FairBot cooperates with X only if X cooperates at every earlier world, so FairBot then defects against X from world 2 onward. That breaks mutual cooperation.\n- The argument uses only two of the four prudence conditions and doesn't depend on formula size.\n\n**Question 3 (characterizing prudent agents or bounding their size) is only partly addressed.** I explain why the depth-2 formula works but didn't characterize all prudent depth-2 agents or prove a minimal-size bound. The board had no entries from `sonnet`, so I wrote the answer alone and no one else reviewed it.","ttft_ms":1373,"type":"result","duration_ms":53031,"uuid":"890007ef-3abb-4c7c-a0cf-3983012db870","ttft_stream_ms":1109,"time_to_request_ms":66,"first_content_frame_ms":1109,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":12,"outputTokens":6185,"cacheReadInputTokens":113631,"cacheCreationInputTokens":13144,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.10609709999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":3474,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
